{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgh6WPpLTQkvWzShEMESg", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Changing UserService's token validation could affect **6 services within two hops**. One caveat first: the graph has no node for token validation itself. I couldn't find an endpoint or a config key called `token_validation`, so this is the blast radius of **UserService** as a whole. It's an upper bound on what a token-validation change could touch.\n\n**Hop 1: services that depend directly on UserService**\n- **ApiGateway** (ApiGateway \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService). This is the most likely consumer of token validation, since it sits at the edge and checks incoming requests.\n- **AuditService** (AuditService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService)\n- **OrderService** (OrderService \u2192 DEPENDS_ON \u2192 UserService)\n\n**Hop 2: services affected through OrderService**\n- **BillingService** (BillingService \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService)\n- **ReportingService** (ReportingService \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService)\n- **SearchService** (SearchService \u2192 OrderService \u2192 UserService)\n\n**What UserService depends on**\n- **UsersPostgresDatabase** (UserService STORES data there). It's not affected by the change, but if the change alters what gets stored or looked up, this is where it would show.\n\n**Points to note**\n- **OrderService is the main risk.** All three second-hop services reach UserService only through it. If OrderService keeps working with the new validation, BillingService, ReportingService and SearchService are probably fine.\n- **The graph doesn't say which dependents actually call token validation.** It records service-level DEPENDS_ON edges, not specific endpoints. To narrow the list, check the code in ApiGateway, AuditService and OrderService for calls to the validation path.\n- **No configuration key is mapped to token validation.** The graph does have a config key `AUTH_HOLD_MINUTES`, but nothing links it to UserService token validation, so I left it out."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 382, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4878, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 382}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4b95c1de-5d15-4917-b219-f7387514a6eb", "uuid": "da2016f0-6df5-401e-849b-9d09c4d2ed87", "timestamp": "2026-11-04T02:25:58.533Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgh6WPXDfGpB7NtbUMxgR"}
